# What does the human actually do?

I would divide human influence into **four moments**.

## Genesis

High influence.

Human sets:

```text
name
appearance
origin
initial personality priors
starter talisman
philosophical/style seed
```

Example:

> Boris values patience, trickery, learning and elegance over brute strength.

These are **priors**, not immutable behavior.

---

# Coaching

Between matches, human can communicate with the Agent.

For example:

> Morty seems to be exploiting your rim movement. What are you going to do about it?

Boris can:

```text
agree
disagree
ask questions
incorporate suggestion
ignore it
```

This is much more interesting than:

```text
human modifies aggression=.72
```

The user is **mentoring an autonomous competitor**.

---

# Engineering

Potentially human participates in body development.

But again, not unrestricted editing.

Maybe:

```text
Boris proposes body changes
Daimon comments
Human allocates development resources
```

For example:

```text
BORIS:
"I need greater center stability."

PENELOPE:
"You're treating the symptom. Morty is manipulating your retreat."

HUMAN:
approves one of three development proposals
```

Now you've got an actual management game.

