# Strategic conversation

Before major matches, the human can talk with Boris.

But the **AI makes the final Battle Avatar**.

This distinction matters enormously.

Human:

> I think Morty expects your usual defensive opening.

Boris:

> Agreed. His last nine matches indicate a 71% early commitment against defensive opponents.

Penelope:

> Then don't merely attack. Let him see the retreat he expects for two seconds.

Boris produces:

```text
battle_avatar_v27
```

Human can inspect the strategic summary.

Then:

```text
LOCK
```

No more intervention.

---

# During the battle: human does nothing

This should be sacred.

```text
NO JOYSTICK
NO BUTTONS
NO MID-BATTLE PROMPTS
NO "USE SUPERPOWER!"
```

Otherwise it becomes another action game.

The tension comes from:

> **We already made our decisions. Now we find out whether our intelligence was good enough.**

Exactly like watching a chess engine, robot competition, horse race, sports team, etc.

The human can only watch.

That makes the match feel legitimate.

