# What does the Daimon do?

This is where I think we should lean back toward your original vision.

Once sufficiently manifested, the Daimon becomes:

```text
advisor
mirror
counterweight
memory interpreter
creative strategist
ability interface
```

It should **not simply agree with the Agent**.

The interesting relationship is:

```text
Agent wants X
Daimon sees Y
```

Because the Daimon is derived from deep behavioral history, it may notice things the Agent's explicit self-model does not.

Example:

> **Boris:** “Morty's mobility is the problem.”

> **Penelope:** “No. You've said that after every loss this season. Your losses occur when you abandon center control after the first collision.”

That is a compelling AI companion.

