# And there is a very cool consequence

RoboBladez starts as:

> **train an AI competitor.**

But after enough history it becomes:

> **raise a persistent artificial character whose identity, relationships, companion and abilities emerge from what it actually experiences.**

The battles are therefore not merely competitions.

They are the environment that produces the characters.

```text
BATTLES
aren't content attached to characters.

BATTLES
are what CREATE the characters.
```

That should probably become one of the project's central theses.

And the Daimon gives you the really unusual version:

> **Every competitor eventually develops an AI companion that is literally generated from the statistical and narrative shape of the life that competitor has lived.**

That is substantially more original than simply giving each AI a mascot.
